// Who made what on the site, and the licences that come with it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Doc from '../components/Doc.astro';
import { company } from '../content/site';
---

<Base title={`Credits & licences — ${company.name}`} description={`The pictures, fonts, paintings and software of the ${company.name} website, and their licences.`}>
  <Doc title="Credits & licences" updated="October 2026">
    <h2>The work</h2>
    <p>
      The photographs show work {company.name} made for its clients. Brand names and logos belong to their owners and are shown as references of that
      work. The pieces shown in 3D in the showrooms are replicas of that same work, modelled from its photographs and printed as it was made.
    </p>
    <h2>The painted scenes</h2>
    <p>
      The animated scenes behind the chapters are adapted, with their creators’ permission, from an existing web experience, and remade for
      {company.name}: every figure is now a white marble statue in the manner of classical Greek sculpture, carrying the studio’s own products (its
      bag, its gift card, its pins, its catalogue, its drawings); the drawing of the 3D chapter is a study after the antique; the animal is now a
      marble Hermes, the messenger, holding up the studio’s box; the shop counter holds the studio’s gift box, with its work framed on the wall;
      and every background is painted anew as a view of Cairo and Egypt.
    </p>
    <p>
      The opening scene is the studio’s own: a photographer and a model holding the studio’s bag, painted for it, with the studio’s work pouring
      out of the bag before a night Egypt. The Partners scene sets the founder in an Egyptian temple hall painted for the studio, and the
      photography chapter is made from Raphael’s portrait of Baldassare Castiglione. Their pictures were raised in depth with Depth Anything V2
      (Apache License 2.0).
    </p>
    <p>
      The repainting was done with Stable Diffusion XL inpainting (Stability AI and Hugging Face, CreativeML Open RAIL++-M licence), guided by
      the scenes’ own drawing through a ControlNet (Hugging Face, CreativeML Open RAIL++-M licence), with the SDXL VAE fp16 fix (MIT licence).
    </p>
    <h2>Paintings</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Raffaello Sanzio (Raphael), <em>The School of Athens</em>, 1509–1511, Apostolic Palace, Vatican City. Public domain.</li>
      <li>Raffaello Sanzio (Raphael), <em>Portrait of Baldassare Castiglione</em>, c. 1514–1515, Musée du Louvre. Public domain.</li>
    </ul>
